{
  "technical_and_design_decisions": [
    "Adopt Docker Compose-style environment variable substitution and --link semantics for the XD container runtime so that bindings to Rabbit, Redis, ZooKeeper, Hadoop, and Mongo can be expressed declaratively.",
    "Use a lightweight, file/YAML-driven service registry (extending servers.yml) rather than introducing a new runtime dependency such as Eureka/Consul for service discovery, keeping the increment compatible with existing embedded-server deployments.",
    "Add a Spring XD admin endpoint and CLI flag that publishes containers into the service registry at startup, so discovery lookups resolve to live containers.",
    "Provide an opt-in CI job (driven by a Jenkinsfile / Maven profile) that produces a base admin image plus per-module derivative images, allowing internal teams to layer their own configurations on top.",
    "Use AsciiDoc for the Mesos/Marathon deployment guide so it can be rendered by the existing Spring documentation tooling.",
    "For RDBMS-to-HDFS partitioning, expose a Strategy interface (Column / Modulo / Custom SpEL) and wire it through the JDBC source module's HDFS sink batch pipeline.",
    "Implement the HDFS source using a polling + listing abstraction (closely mirroring the existing file source) and reuse the existing OOTB source contract to minimize downstream changes.",
    "Add a top-level `spring.xd.job.commitInterval` property to servers.yml and propagate it through the JobLauncher and partition-aware batch jobs, preserving the existing default if not set.",
    "Use Java 17 (the minimum for Spring Framework 6.x) and assume the work is performed on the Spring XD 1.x / Spring Cloud Data Flow line where applicable."
  ],
  "assumptions": [
    "Estimates assume a single senior Java/Spring developer working full-time (8-hour workday) with solid familiarity with Spring XD internals, Docker, and Hadoop tooling.",
    "Test infrastructure (Rabbit, Redis, ZooKeeper, Hadoop, Mongo, HDFS, RDBMS, Mesos/Marathon) is already available in the CI environment; no time is allocated to provisioning it from scratch.",
    "Each activity's estimate includes the time to write unit tests; a separate cross-cutting integration testing activity is included for end-to-end validation across stories.",
    "Dependency-upgrade evaluation (U5) is scoped to identifying breaking changes, applying upgrades in a feature branch, and running the existing test suite—not to fixing unrelated regressions uncovered by the upgrade.",
    "Docker image CI build (U3) is scoped to the admin image and one representative module image to prove the pipeline; productionizing the pipeline for every module is out of scope.",
    "Documentation activities produce reference docs in the existing project structure; no translation or external publishing work is included.",
    "No performance tuning, large-scale load testing, or production rollout/operations work is included beyond what is required to validate each feature.",
    "The HDFS source module is implemented for the most common cases (HDFS over file:// / hdfs:// URIs with simple text/sequence file ingestion); a full Hadoop FileFormat plug-in system is out of scope."
  ],
  "activities": [
    {
      "activity_id": "A0",
      "activity_name": "Requirements analysis and overall design",
      "activity_description": "Review the eight user stories, clarify ambiguities, define module boundaries, agree on the configuration schema extensions (servers.yml), and produce a short technical design note that drives the implementation activities below.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A1",
      "activity_name": "U1 - Docker XD container service linking",
      "activity_description": "Extend the XD container launcher to support Docker-style --link semantics and environment-variable interpolation so that containers can bind to external Rabbit, Redis, ZooKeeper, Hadoop, and Mongo services. Update the admin UI/CLI to expose the new attributes and ship unit + integration tests against at least two of the target services.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A2",
      "activity_name": "U2 - Service discovery configuration for XD containers",
      "activity_description": "Add a service registry backed by the existing servers.yml configuration. Implement admin/CLI commands to register a container at startup and a client-side discovery abstraction that jobs and modules can use to resolve other services by logical name.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A3",
      "activity_name": "U3 - Docker image build via CI",
      "activity_description": "Author a Dockerfile and a CI pipeline (Jenkinsfile / Maven build profile) that produces a base XD admin image, demonstrates a module-derivative image, runs the standard test suite inside the image, and publishes images to a local registry as part of the build.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A4",
      "activity_name": "U4 - Mesos + Marathon deployment guide",
      "activity_description": "Write an AsciiDoc reference guide describing how to deploy an XD cluster on Mesos using Marathon, covering container layout, network ports, persistent volumes for ZooKeeper/HDFS state, and recommended instance counts and constraints.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A5",
      "activity_name": "U5 - Spring Boot dependency upgrade evaluation",
      "activity_description": "Bump Spring Boot (and related Spring Framework) dependencies to the target version in a feature branch, run the existing unit and integration test suites, and produce a short report listing behavioral changes, deprecated APIs, and recommended follow-up actions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A6",
      "activity_name": "U6 - Data partitioning strategy for RDBMS -> HDFS ingest",
      "activity_description": "Introduce a PartitionStrategy interface (Column, Modulo, and Custom SpEL implementations) on the JDBC source, wire it through to the HDFS batch sink, expose a servers.yml / job-parameter configuration surface, and add tests that verify parallel ingest produces non-overlapping partitions.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A7",
      "activity_name": "U7 - HDFS source module",
      "activity_description": "Implement a new OOTB HDFS source module that lists files under a configurable path (HDFS or file:// URI), emits file contents as messages, and supports basic options (filePattern, time/byte rollovers, completion marker handling). Include unit tests with the MiniHDFSCluster and a small integration test against a real HDFS instance.",
      "most_likely_effort": 3.5
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A8",
      "activity_name": "U8 - Configurable commit interval via servers.yml",
      "activity_description": "Add a `spring.xd.job.commitInterval` property to servers.yml, plumb it through the JobLauncher and every OOTB job that supports partitioning, ensure the existing default is preserved when the property is absent, and add tests for both the default and override paths.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A9",
      "activity_name": "Cross-cutting integration testing",
      "activity_description": "Run end-to-end integration scenarios that combine the new features (e.g., an HDFS-source job with custom partitioning and an overridden commit interval running in linked containers) and capture results for release notes.",
      "most_likely_effort": 2.0
    },
    {
      "activity_id": "A10",
      "activity_name": "Documentation, code review follow-ups, and release prep",
      "activity_description": "Update user-facing reference docs (configuration, new source module, service linking/discovery) to reflect the increment, address code review comments on each change set, and prepare release notes summarizing the new and changed features.",
      "most_likely_effort": 1.5
    }
  ],
  "reported_total": {
    "most_likely_effort": 24.0
  }
}
```

